        "title": "Residues, Poles, and Laurent Series",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The residue theorem is the master tool of complex integration. It reduces contour integrals — and by extension, many difficult real integrals — to the algebraic task of computing residues at isolated singularities. Laurent series are the mechanism: they extend Taylor series to handle singularities, and the residue is simply the coefficient of 1/(z − a) in the Laurent expansion."
